<exercisegroup cols="2" xml:id="exercisegroup-matrix-ops-verify-rules">
<title>Verifying matrix algebra rules</title>

<introduction>

	<p>
	Practise verifying matrix algebra rules.
	Use the provided proofs of
	<xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules-basic-add-assoc">Rule</xref>
	and
	<xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules-scalar-mul-scalar-matrix-mult-assoc-1">Rule</xref>
	from <xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules" />
	as templates/guides to carrying out your own verifications.
	You may also find your answers to
	<xref first="exercise-matrix-ops-entry-patterns-add" last="exercise-matrix-ops-entry-patterns-power">Exercises</xref> helpful.
	</p>

	<p> <alert>Recall.</alert> The symbol <m>\zerovec</m> represents a zero matrix of appropriate dimensions, not the scalar <m>0</m>. </p>

</introduction>

<exercise><p> <xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules-zero-add"                   >Rule</xref>. </p></exercise>
<exercise><p> Rule: <m> A + A = 2 A</m> for every matrix <m>A</m>.                                      </p></exercise>
<exercise><p> Rule: <m> 1 A = A    </m> for every matrix <m>A</m>.                                      </p></exercise>
<exercise><p> <xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules-distrib-scalar-mul-over-add">Rule</xref>. </p></exercise>
<exercise><p> <xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules-zero-mult-left"             >Rule</xref>. </p></exercise>
<exercise><p> <xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules-basic-left-distrib"         >Rule</xref>. </p></exercise>

<exercise xml:id="exercise-matrix-ops-verify-rules-zero-row-product"><p>
	Rule:
	if matrix <m>A</m> has a row that is all zeros,
	then so does the product <m> A B </m> for every matrix <m>B</m> for which the product is defined.
</p></exercise>

<exercise xml:id="exercise-matrix-ops-verify-rules-zero-col-product"><p>
	Rule:
	if matrix <m>B</m> has a column that is all zeros,
	then so does the product <m> A B </m> for every matrix <m>A</m> for which the product is defined.
</p></exercise>

<exercise><p> <xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules-transpose-transpose"        >Rule</xref>. </p></exercise>
<exercise><p> <xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules-transpose-add"              >Rule</xref>. </p></exercise>
<exercise><p> <xref ref="proposition-matrix-ops-algebra-rules-transpose-smul"             >Rule</xref>. </p></exercise>

</exercisegroup>
